    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\alpha=60^\\circ$.\n\nUse $\\alpha+2\\beta=180^\\circ$ and the tangent double-angle identity.",
      "worked": "The base angles are equal, so $\\alpha+2\\beta=180^\\circ$ and $0^\\circ<\\beta<90^\\circ$. Since $\\tan\\beta>0$ and $\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta=3$, $\\alpha$ is acute; hence $45^\\circ<\\beta<90^\\circ$.\n\nLet $u=\\tan\\beta>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta&=3\\\\\n\\tan(180^\\circ-2\\beta)\\tan\\beta&=3\\\\\n-\\tan2\\beta\\tan\\beta&=3\\\\\n-\\frac{2u^2}{1-u^2}&=3\\\\\n-2u^2&=3-3u^2\\\\\nu^2&=3\\\\\nu&=\\sqrt3\\\\\n\\beta&=60^\\circ\\\\\n\\alpha&=180^\\circ-2(60^\\circ)\\\\\n\\alpha&=60^\\circ\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
